One that I think is missing is Gurthang (Iron of Death), Turin Turambar's
sword in _The_Silmarillion_.  It was made out of the metal in a meteorite,
and was able to cut through ordinary metals.  When used, it should destroy
any armor that the monster is wearing, which would help you to kill it,
but wouldn't leave you anything to pick off the corpse, armor-wise.
Also, when wielded, you wouldn't get a warning message when attacking
a peaceful creature.

Oh, yeah, it's a two-handed sword, and should be neutral or chaotic.

